WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:24.500
HBO is developing a new Game of Thrones prequel
show based on George R.R. Martin’s Tales

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.970
of Dunk and Egg, which follow the adventures
of Ser Duncan the Tall (Dunk) and young Aegon

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:36.050
V Targaryen (Egg) 90 years prior to the events
of “A Song of Ice and Fire.” To some of

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:41.079
you, this might come as a huge, unexpected
surprise, but I've been waiting for this confirmation

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:47.360
for quite some time. On February 10th, 2013,
George R.R. Martin confirmed that he’d been

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.980
in discussion with HBO over a possible adaptation
of the Tales of Dunk and Egg short stories

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.740
and ever since I knew it would sooner or later
be official.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:02.290
The Game of Thrones ended in 2019. The Game
of Thrones prequel series, House of the Dragon,

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:07.920
will air in 2022. And now, Variety reports
that HBO is in early stages of developing

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.040
another, as-yet unnamed spinoff show based
on George R.R. Martin’s Tales of Dunk and

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.450
Egg. The Tales of Dunk and Egg is an ongoing
series of prequel novellas written by George

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:24.119
R. R. Martin, set in the world of A Song of
Ice and Fire. The stories relate the adventures

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:29.250
of the hedge knight Ser Duncan the Tall, who
would become a legendary member of the Kingsguard,

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:35.350
and his squire Egg, who would become King
Aegon V Targaryen of Westeros. Although Egg

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:40.820
is a boy at the start of the series, he will
eventually grow up to become King Aegon V,

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.289
or "Aegon the Unlikely". The stories begin
with their meeting 90 years before the events

00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:51.149
of Game of Thrones, and may cover the events
until the deaths of Duncan and King Aegon.

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:55.750
Martin has published three novellas in the
“Tales of Dunk and Egg” series to date:

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:02.590
“The Hedge Knight” in 1998, “The Sworn
Sword” in 2003, and “The Mystery Knight”

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:05.350
in 2010.
The three novellas were then collected and

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:11.200
published together as “A Knight of the Seven
Kingdoms” in 2015. The Tales of Dunk and

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.390
Egg begin 90 years before the War of the Five
Kings,

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:19.480
at the end of the reign of King Daeron II
Targaryen. The realm is still recovering from

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:24.820
the First Blackfyre Rebellion thirteen years
before, a great civil war that tore the Seven

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:30.790
Kingdoms in half. Daeron II's bastard half-brother
Daemon Blackfyre had tried to seize the throne

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:36.590
in the rebellion, but was killed in the final
battle of the war. Several of his sons survived

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.780
by fleeing into exile, and across the Narrow
Sea, House Blackfyre is continually plotting

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:48.019
all manner of intrigues against the main branch
of the Targaryen dynasty, hoping to gain support

00:02:48.019 --> 00:02:53.550
for new rebellions. The Targaryens are still
having difficulty maintaining their hold on

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:58.470
power, particularly since the last of their
dragons died fifty years ago, and the beasts

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:03.360
are starting to fade from living memory. There
are also lingering tensions from the recent

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.959
unification of Dorne with the rest of the
Seven Kingdoms. The fiercely independent Dornishmen

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:14.200
had resisted Targaryen conquest for two centuries,
and only finally came under the authority

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:20.159
of the Iron Throne through peaceful marriage-alliance.
Daeron II married the sister of the Prince

00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:25.110
of Dorne, and Daeron II's sister married the
Prince of Dorne. The terms of the alliance

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:30.349
led to the Iron Throne giving House Martell
of Dorne preferential treatment, with a strong

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:35.560
pro-Martell faction developing around Daeron
II at the royal court. This is one of the

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:41.329
factors that sparked the Blackfyre Rebellion,
as all of the non-Dornish lords who felt that

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:46.290
the pro-Martell faction was receiving royal
favors which should have been theirs ultimately

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:52.280
sided with Daemon Blackfyre. Despite thirteen
years of relative peace, relations between

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.031
the Dornish and the rest of the Seven Kingdoms
remain tenuous. Worse problems are on the

00:03:57.031 --> 00:04:02.659
horizon, as during the course of Dunk and
Egg's first adventures a massive plague known

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:07.389
as the Great Spring Sickness sweeps across
the Seven Kingdoms (Westeros' equivalent of

00:04:07.389 --> 00:04:12.639
the Black Death), upsetting what was already
a fragile political balance. With plague and

00:04:12.639 --> 00:04:17.910
drought devastating the Seven Kingdoms, many
turn to banditry to survive, and the roads

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:23.870
are crawling with outlaw bands. Petty feuds
erupt between local lords competing over food

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:29.300
and resources. With the realm weakened from
within, dangers arise on every side,

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:34.460
as the Targaryens' enemies see their vulnerable
state as a perfect opportunity to attack.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:39.660
Besides the continuing tensions with the Dornish
to the south, the Blackfyres across the eastern

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:44.630
sea are attempting to raise new armies in
the Free Cities, and to turn lords in Westeros

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:50.270
to their side who are upset at the difficulties
the Targaryen reign is encountering. To the

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:54.740
west, the ironborn led by Dagon Greyjoy are
seizing their best chance in generations to

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.990
return to the Old Way, conducting brazen coastal
raids from Bear Island in the North to The

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:06.080
Arbor in the south. To the north the wildlings
have been united by a new King-Beyond-the-Wall,

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.630
Raymun Redbeard, and they are preparing to
cross over the Wall and sweep through the

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:16.610
lands to the south. Into this backdrop steps
Ser Duncan the Tall, a very large squire who

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:21.230
grew up as an orphan in the slums of Flea
Bottom in King's Landing. A hedge knight,

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:26.920
Ser Arlan of Pennytree, has died during the
night. His squire, a large young man named

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:33.320
Dunk, buries him and pays his last respects.
After considering several options, Dunk decides

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:38.630
to continue his journey to Ashford and compete
in the tourney as a knight. He adopts Ser

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:44.510
Arlan's armor as his own, as well as his equipment,
three horses, and remaining monies. At an

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:49.800
inn on the road, he meets a boy with a shaved
head named Egg who secretly follows him to

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:55.940
Ashford. Impressed by the boy's spirit, Dunk
takes him on as his own squire for the upcoming

00:05:55.940 --> 00:06:01.020
tourney. At Ashford, Dunk sells one of his
horses to commission armor, then attempts

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:05.990
to enter the lists of the tourney. Without
proof of his knighthood, he’s nearly barred

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:11.100
from competition until Prince Baelor Targaryen
vouches for him. Dunk watches the first day

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:17.460
of competition amongst the commoners, with
Egg on his shoulders. After several spectacular

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:24.230
tilts, the day ends when Prince Aerion Targaryen
disgraces himself by killing Ser Humfrey Hardyng's

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:29.840
horse. That night, Egg informs Dunk that a
puppeteer girl he had met earlier is being

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:35.840
beaten by Prince Aerion. Dunk leaps to her
defense and attacks Aerion, striking him in

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:42.520
the face. As a royal guard arrests Dunk, Egg
reveals himself to be Aerion's brother, Prince

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:49.480
Aegon Targaryen, commonly known by his nickname
"Egg", a grandson of King Daeron II. In jail,

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:54.150
Dunk chooses to take a trial by combat rather
than losing his hand.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:59.230
Prince Aerion demands the combat to be a Trial
of Seven, as his brother, Prince Daeron, also

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:04.940
accused Dunk of kidnapping Aegon from his
charge. Dunk must find six champions to fight

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:10.630
with him against seven accusing knights, or
he will forfeit. Steffon Fossoway is the first

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:16.040
ally - Dunk finds - and he and Egg bring more
champions to Dunk’s cause. The fourteen

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:21.970
champions line their mounts - along opposite
sides of the tourney grounds and charge. Dunk

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:28.430
tilts against Aerion, but is quickly unhorsed.
Altough nearly defeated, Dunk manages to grapple

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:34.220
Aerion and use his size advantage to pummel
Aerion into submission. Aerion recants his

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:39.620
accusation, ending the Trial. The fighting
costs the lives of both Humphreys. Prince

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:46.100
Baelor, who had not brought his own armor,
but instead wore armor made for his son, took

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:51.510
a blow to the head from a mace. After the
battle, Baelor approaches Dunk to congratulate

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:56.960
him, and begins to act drunkenly. When his
crushed helm is removed, it’s shown that

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.500
the weaker armor made for his son did not
protect him from the blow which has crushed

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.990
in his skull. Aerion's father, Maekar, meets
with Dunk after the funeral, revealing that

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:12.720
it was his mace that killed Baelor.
He regrets Aerion's behavior and offers Dunk

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:18.751
a position in his household to train Aegon.
Dunk insists on being allowed to travel, and

00:08:18.751 --> 00:08:24.370
offers to take Aegon as his squire to learn
to be a better knight than Aerion. Maekar

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:30.960
agrees, making sure Aegon continues to use
his alias of Egg to avoid scandal. Dunk and

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:36.610
Egg set out to Dorne, in search of the puppeteer
whom Dunk had saved. Through a series of many

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:41.390
adventures the unlikely duo of "Dunk and Egg"
will, in the course of years, rise to great

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:47.771
fame, as Egg grows to become King Aegon V,
and Dunk becomes Ser Duncan the Tall, Lord

00:08:47.771 --> 00:08:53.140
Commander of the Kingsguard. Martin has said
that the novellas will include time-jumps

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:57.860
so that they will ultimately cover the rest
of the lives of the two main characters, stretching

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:03.511
across a period of 50 years, until both of
them die in the Tragedy of Summerhall. This

00:09:03.511 --> 00:09:09.640
will bridge the timeline between the two main
narrative eras: Ser Barristan Selmy was knighted

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:16.370
at the age of sixteen by King Aegon V after
unhorsing Ser Duncan in a joust. Tywin Lannister's

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:21.690
grandfather Gerold Lannister is a character
in the early novellas, but young Tywin was

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:28.370
a boy when Aegon V died. Prince Rhaegar Targaryen
was also born the very same night as the Tragedy

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:34.150
at Summerhall. No writer or talent is currently
attached to the project, but sources say it’s

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:39.760
a high priority for HBO as the premium cabler
looks to build on the success of “Game of

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.570
Thrones.” Should the project go to series,
it would be the second “Game of Thrones”

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:49.371
prequel to make it to screen. The network
is currently prepping the series “House

00:09:49.371 --> 00:09:55.380
of the Dragon,” which is slated to debut
in 2022. That show will document the buildup

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:00.520
to the Targaryen civil war in Westeros that’s
known as the Dance of Dragons.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:05.890
Fans have been calling for a “Tales of Dunk
and Egg” TV series for some time now and

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:11.500
now we might finally get it. It’s important
to note that HBO has just started developing

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.080
this show,
but it's good to know that we'll get more

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:19.001
of Westeros and its stories. In the meantime,
we have another Game of Thrones prequel, House

00:10:19.001 --> 00:10:24.060
of the Dragon, to keep us in touch with the
magic world of Westeros, which will be about

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:29.330
Targaryen history and which is going to air
in 2022. Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:33.710
and let me know which Game of Thrones prequel
excites you more; Tales of Dunk and Egg or

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:38.450
House of the Dragon. If you enjoyed this video
please give it a big thumbs up and I hope

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:44.450
to see you in the next one. Peace!

